## Observed Behavior
<!--
Please describe the problem you saw. Include waveforms (in VCD or Verilator/GtkWave FST format only please) and log files if possible.
-->
While testing single-step behaviour, a cosimulation-mismatch was encountered when reading DCSR.cause. It was tracked down to a simultaneous assertion of DCSR.step and debug_req_i when entering debug_mode, and I believe that the spike behaviour is correct in this case.
According to both debug specifications [0.13.2](https://riscv.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/riscv-debug-release.pdf) and [1.0.0-STABLE](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/riscv/riscv-debug-spec/master/riscv-debug-stable.pdf), the priority among reporting DCSR.cause has **step** (0) as a lower priority than **haltreq** (1). Ibex [currently reports](https://ibex-core.readthedocs.io/en/latest/03_reference/debug.html#debug-support) debug support in compliance with the RISCV Debug Specification Version 0.13.
Current ibex behaviour is a priority-encoder [which places **step** above **haltreq**](https://github.com/lowRISC/ibex/blob/c4a97e05f5853b25e40fa1ea5b4edcfafba9a370/rtl/ibex_controller.sv#L662).


## Expected Behavior
<!-- Please describe the behavior you expected to see instead. -->
Ibex should prioritize reporting DCSR.cause as **haltreq** above **step** when entering debug_mode with both stimulus present.
